					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/electro-daddy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3126543); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3126543&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607373916" alt="Electro_Daddy" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3126543)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/electro-daddy" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3126543); return false;" >Electro_Daddy</a></span> <span class="odate time_1496267613 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">31 May 2017 21:53</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2838144">
									

<p>I liked it for the most part. Being a fan of Exploration Logs and all. But I can't shake the feeling that something is off about the tone in the logs. Maybe try and be more clinical if possible, it felt like I was being rushed though the worlds you created. They were interesting to me and I feel they would benefit from more description, more &quot;exploration&quot; if you will.</p>
<p>Also I would change a few of the D Classes quotes. I felt some of them convey very unnecessary information. I'd like to &quot;hear&quot; more about what they see and are experiencing and less what they had to say in the moment.</p>
<p>A final critique would be the use of the word &quot;they&quot; when referring to the D-Class. I get what you mean but it degrades the clinical tone a little and kept making me think there was more then 1 D-class present. Maybe be more specific about the test subject in question, like denoting their age and gender at the beginning of the log so you can use a more specific pronoun that doesn't imply an additional person is present.</p>
<p>That aside I enjoyed it except for the few things I mention that bothered me. I'll +1 because of the potential.</p>

							</div>

								
